# arms/wireless

Deterministic wireless-retail math for the T-Mobile-style store `store_tmobile`: service plans, multi-line pricing,
device financing, trade-in estimates, promotion eligibility, accessory compatibility, a household plan optimizer and
full cart quotes that keep upfront charges apart from monthly ones. No LLM: the assistant and the web app only show
and phrase what this arm computes.

**All prices, credits, trade-in values and financing terms are synthetic demo data** (`data/wireless.yaml`), not real
T-Mobile offers, approved financing or real trade-in quotes. Device and accessory list prices come from the catalog
(`data/products.yaml`); people and accounts are fictional.

## Scope (CLAUDE.md §3)

Store `store_tmobile` only; the grocery stores never call this arm.

- [x] Plans: advertised price per line count, autopay adjustment, taxes & fees estimate, eligibility (55+) (fake)
- [x] Plan comparison for N lines, cheapest eligible first (fake)
- [x] Financing: 24/36 months at 0% APR (demo), down payment, financing cap, rounding into the last installment (fake)
- [x] Promotions: device credits, trade-in bonus, switcher, line discount, accessory bundle, protection, home
      internet, dated sales; applied only when every condition is met, otherwise reported with the unmet ones (fake)
- [x] Trade-in: value by condition, balance still owed from the account, bonus, honest `keep_recommended` (young
      phone, balance > value, a sale on the target within 60 days) (fake)
- [x] Household optimizer: cheapest plan that fits the heaviest line's data + hotspot; "keep your plan" is a valid
      answer, and so is "this costs more but fits" (fake)
- [x] Compatible accessories for a device, with live store stock; always optional (fake)
- [x] Cart quote: devices, accessories, plan, new-line fees, add-ons, trade-in, est. taxes; upfront vs monthly; total
      over the term; stock checks; errors and compatibility warnings instead of exceptions (fake)
- [ ] Cart Whisperer cards from these signals (recommender arm, contracts v0.3)

## Contract

`contracts/wireless.py` and `contracts.services.WirelessService` (0.2.3, `contracts/CHANGES-0.2.3.md`). REST is in
`contracts/api.md` ("wireless retail"), served by `arms/gateway/wireless_api.py`.

## Files

- `engine.py`: the pure pricing engine (`WirelessEngine`), no I/O.
- `service.py`: `BaseWirelessService` + the real `WirelessService` (prices and stock from `services.catalog` at call
  time, so robot picks and restocks show up in the next quote).
- `fake.py`: `FakeWirelessService` (same engine; prices from `data/products.yaml`, stock as shipped in the planogram).
- `data.py`: loads and validates `data/wireless.yaml` (`contracts.wireless.WirelessFile`).

## How to run

Base deps only; no keys.

```bash
uv run pytest arms/wireless arms/gateway/tests/test_wireless_api.py
PICKY_REAL_ARMS=wireless,catalog make dev    # real: live catalog prices + stock; leave it out for the fake
```

Fallback flag: drop `wireless` from `PICKY_REAL_ARMS` (the fake uses the same engine and data).

## Demo-ready checklist (CLAUDE.md §6)

- [x] Implements `WirelessService` fully; no `NotImplementedError` on demo paths
- [x] Predictable failures degrade: unknown sku/plan, out of stock, too many lines, ineligible promo → `errors` in the
      quote; 404 / 409 / 422 on the single-purpose routes
- [x] Switchable to the fake by env flag alone
- [x] Tests for the core math pass
- [ ] `make demo` exercises it (the scripted demo trip is grocery; the T-Mobile flow is the web app's `/plans` + the
      store_tmobile robot order)

## Known limitations

- Taxes are a flat estimate (`tax_rate_bps`, `service_taxes_fees_bps`); no per-jurisdiction rules.
- One trade-in per quote; protection is counted per phone in the cart (min 1).
- Promo credits are spread evenly with the remainder dropped (at most a few cents); installments put the remainder in
  the last month.
- "today" is fixed in `data/wireless.yaml` so the promo windows (WAIT) are repeatable in the demo.
